      "writtenOn": "2023-10-17T18:14:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reason we clear the directory is that there are cases where the output files are headers, and clang can only take a directory, not a list of files to use as headers.  If we don\u0027t clear the directory then any files that are no longer generated by the rule could be left behind.  If those old files are headers that are still referenced in other source files then incremental builds will succeed, but a clean build will fail.",
      "parentUuid": "261ffe0c_30c92347",
